#: ../../catalog_intake.md:156 006c2917aee043be9791b26c15f97095
msgid "Label OCR (`api/services/label_ocr.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:158 34c25cb8e711449ea0b1dcc1687ea972
msgid ""
"The app sends each receiving photo right after it is stored (every kind: "
"the label's fields are used now, the other photos' text feeds the "
"reference suggestion's fallback pass); capture never waits. "
"`run_label_ocr` (Celery) posts the image to the `ocr` sidecar (`ocr/`: "
"RapidOCR, i.e. PaddleOCR models on ONNX Runtime, CPU, about 1 s per "
"label), then extracts candidates from the text lines in reading order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:164 084c8d3227d142ae8e0e1cea99288e78
msgid "**serial**, from the surest to the least sure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:165 27bfffd64160400aac6a8342bc93fd34
msgid ""
"value after `SN:` (the usual form), `S/N`, `Serial No.` (also as the OCR "
"misreads it: `Serlal`, `Seria1`), `N° de série`, `Serien-Nr.`, "
"`Ser.-Nr.`... (same line or the line below, or glued to the previous "
"value: `ECN:390-1544SN:ICV18230008`), containing at least one digit;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:169 d79828c194ac4c378b45b688e583f4f3
msgid "a line starting with `N:` (a cut `S/N:`), at half confidence;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:170 2985f16f136d4c4f822c0af83bf0fab8
msgid ""
"a word that only *looks like* a serial label (approximate match with "
"`serial`, `seriennummer`, `numéro de série`..., e.g. `SeralHo.:`), at 0.8"
" x confidence, flagged ``guess``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:173 fc2e239d8f9b4c0fb0542b9054c1214a
msgid ""
"no label at all: the token shaped most like a serial (digits, letters and"
" digits mixed, 8-14 characters), skipping ratings (`220V-240V`), dates, "
"file names, addresses and model / part / contact lines, at 0.3 x "
"confidence, flagged ``guess``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:177 a744e859a4014909b8d06dff664ed23e
msgid ""
"**model**: value after `Model` / `Model No.`, `Type`, `Device`, `Réf.`; "
"only without one of these, `Cat. No.`, `P/N`, `Part No.`, `Art.-Nr.`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:179 183c4df980884d2b85be873f644a8c6c
msgid "**brand**: the longest Airtable `Marque` name found as a word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:181 92f8faf194964d329f8953d99edfc336
msgid ""
"Each comes with the OCR confidence and the line it was read from; "
"`fields` also holds the whole `text` in reading order. Nothing is written"
" to Airtable. The task retries (3 times) when the sidecar is unreachable "
"or slow. The sidecar is internal (`OCR_URL`, default `http://ocr:8000`); "
"CI builds and pushes it as `ghcr.io/<repo>-ocr` with the same tags as the"
" API image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:187 f7d963ff977b4a8db289b1c55679819c
msgid "AI product research (`api/services/product_research.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:189 1c43d28287034a77ad1d9493d5b165bb
msgid ""
"Started by the app when operations mark a reception done: one job per "
"distinct product identity (brand + model read on the labels, else the "
"reprise equipment row or the devis line). Celery task "
"`run_product_research`. Two calls through the AI service, each on the "
"feature's chain of AI models (default: Claude Opus 5.5, then Sonnet 5.5, "
"then OpenRouter once configured):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:195 c0280ae5752f4f489b9d25613d7ce2be
msgid ""
"**research**: web search with adaptive thinking and high effort (Claude: "
"server-side `web_search` + `web_fetch`, `pause_turn` resumed up to 4 "
"times; OpenRouter: the `web` plugin); the model writes notes with a "
"source URL per fact and lists PDF datasheets/manuals;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:199 a029e956cc2a4c59906d2c1620f422b3
msgid ""
"**extraction**: notes -> strict JSON schema: French short and long "
"descriptions, specifications **using existing `Specification type` names "
"only** (anything else goes to `unmapped_facts`, enforced again in code), "
"dimensions (mm) and weight (kg), documents, sources (plus the web results"
" seen), confidence and `missing` fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:205 343e96a0169747fc9e931d2c32cade30
msgid ""
"The result also carries the research `notes`, `ai_call_id` (the "
"extraction, for feedback), `ai_call_ids` and `ai_models`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:208 99da9249b69d40dc837b00354cfb199a
msgid ""
"A proposal only: nothing is written to Airtable here; the commercial team"
" creates the product from it in the app and reviews every value. Web "
"content is treated as data, never as instructions. The job fails when the"
" whole chain is unavailable (every AI model skipped or failed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:213 10b2827c266f4c8bb3cf5a0a1b8db0e0
msgid "Central AI service (`api/services/ai/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:215 bc068e80026f47758fe6c3fa4e4ef42d
msgid ""
"Every AI call of the API goes through `AIService.run(feature, request)`: "
"one provider-neutral request (`AIRequest`: system prompt, text, image and"
" PDF parts, optional JSON schema, web search, thinking, effort) tried on "
"the feature's **chain of AI models**, in order, until one answers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:220 21467e78433e4db89c251426ec199bcc
msgid ""
"**Providers** (`providers/`): `anthropic` (Anthropic SDK, Messages API) "
"and `openrouter` (chat completions, `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`). Keys"
" come from the environment only (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or "
"`ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`). Each provider translates "
"the request (images, PDF, JSON schema, web search, effort) and maps its "
"errors to one code: `rate_limited`, `no_credit`, `overloaded`, `timeout`,"
" `connection`, `bad_request`, `refused`, `invalid_response`, `truncated`,"
" `error`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:227 0616bf19143a4a0bb408a56008433749
msgid ""
"**AI models** (`ModelProfile`, editable in the app's `/settings/ia`): an "
"id, a label, a provider and its model id (e.g. `claude-opus-5-5`, "
"`openai/gpt-5.2`), an optional manual price (USD per million tokens, "
"input and output; overrides the list price in Anthropic cost estimates; 0"
" and 0 = **free**), on/off, **directives** appended to every request it "
"serves, effort and max output tokens overrides, capabilities (reads "
"images, web search, structured JSON) and its own limits (calls per day, "
"monthly budget). Several AI models may share a provider model with "
"different directives. Defaults: `claude-opus`, `claude-sonnet` (both with"
" web search), `claude-haiku`, and `openrouter` (disabled until a model id"
" is set)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:238 c65ce8e6648347a385f3ca53163f9236
msgid ""
"**Chains:** each feature lists AI model ids in priority order. An AI "
"model is **skipped** when it is disabled, its provider is disabled or has"
" no key, it lacks a capability the feature requires (`product_research` "
"and `document_search`: web + JSON; `reference_suggestion`, "
"`description_writing` and `pdf_extraction`: JSON; images are dropped for "
"models without vision), or one of its limits is reached (model or "
"provider daily calls / monthly budget, global budget). Free AI models "
"skip every budget check, and a feature stays available past the global "
"budget while its chain holds an enabled free model. It **fails over** to "
"the next on any provider error, an invalid JSON answer or a JSON answer "
"cut by the token limit (`truncated`) — without retrying it, except after "
"a **rate limit** (429): the AI model then cools down "
"(`general.retry_after_seconds`, 30 s, or its own `retry_after_seconds`) "
"while the next usable model is tried at once; when only cooling models "
"are left, the service waits for the first one and tries it again, up to "
"`general.rate_limit_retries` new tries per model and "
"`general.max_wait_seconds` of waiting per request (≤ 240 s, under the "
"app's HTTP timeout). Cooldowns carry over between requests and processes "
"(read from the call log). When nothing answers, `AIUnavailable` lists "
"every attempt and its reason (synchronous routes answer 502; an async job"
" fails; the reference suggestion falls back to its heuristic ranking)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:258 5cb3867a78a346cfb6d80f98fe08ff64
msgid ""
"**Limits and budgets** (provider, AI model, feature, global): empty "
"(``None``) = no limit, ``0`` = a real zero (no calls / nothing to spend)."
" Settings version 2 used ``0`` for \"no limit\" and are migrated to "
"``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:261 207ac6e830c8441f90fb97bc66c16320
msgid ""
"**Feature settings:** on/off, chain, daily call limit, image analysis and"
" max images (reference suggestion: also `suggestions` and "
"`ocr_fallback`), plus a global monthly budget (default 100 USD); these "
"are checked before the chain (`AIBlocked`: 503 `not_configured`, 409 "
"`disabled`, 429 `daily_limit` / `budget`) and blocked attempts are "
"recorded as `blocked`. Default daily limits: `product_research` 50, "
"`reference_suggestion` 300 (2 images), `description_writing` 200, "
"`document_search` and `pdf_extraction` 100. Settings v1 (one model per "
"feature) are migrated on read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:270 bce356a247734ac9903f02e51c149cba
msgid ""
"**Recorded per attempt** (SQLite `AI_DB_PATH`, default "
"`/home/rewake/DB/ai.sqlite`): feature, provider, AI model, served model, "
"tokens (input, output, cache read/write), web searches, images, cost "
"(Anthropic: estimated at list prices; OpenRouter: the `usage.cost` it "
"bills), duration, status, error code, request id and subject. Limit skips"
" are recorded as `blocked`; configuration skips are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:276 e2f1c4110f414be0b22ee507d312008d
msgid ""
"**Feedback:** results the app shows are reported back as `accepted` / "
"`edited` / `rejected`, giving each feature's acceptance rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:278 dc2b2ead1a664dfba6aa9bfc4e1a464c
msgid ""
"**Errors:** stored as `code: message`; OpenRouter errors carry the "
"upstream provider and its own reason (`metadata.raw`, also for errors "
"returned with HTTP 200), invalid JSON keeps the start of the answer. A "
"failed or limit-skipped attempt points to the call that answered instead "
"(`fallback_call_id`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:283 d7041ad04dcf45f8836e03d53956321e
msgid ""
"**Test:** `POST /internal/ai/models/test` (an AI model, saved or not) "
"sends a tiny real request — \"pong\", a red test image if it reads "
"images, a JSON schema if structured — and returns the answer, checks, "
"served model, duration, cost and the catalog entry (or close ids). "
"Recorded as feature `model_test` (`model_test.py`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:288 8320e32624c246b3aa460b81e1836bbb
msgid ""
"**Routes** (`/internal/ai/*`): `GET/PUT /settings` (GET adds which "
"providers have a key, each feature's label and requirements, and the "
"price `catalog` in USD per million tokens: Anthropic list prices, "
"OpenRouter's public `/api/v1/models` cached 6 h — `pricing.py`; PUT "
"validates ids and chains and rejects unknown fields, 422), `GET "
"/usage?days=` (per feature, per provider + AI model, per day), `GET "
"/calls?limit=&feature=`, `POST /feedback` (`call_id`, `outcome`, optional"
" `detail`), `POST /models/test`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:296 88d06b5463dd4374b0efbcda3e101a8b
msgid ""
"**Token limit and reasoning:** a reasoning model spends hidden reasoning "
"tokens within its output limit. On OpenRouter the limit sent is twice the"
" answer's (`max_tokens`), with reasoning capped at the answer's size "
"(`reasoning.max_tokens`) unless the AI model sets an effort or the "
"request asks for thinking (then `reasoning.effort`); a JSON answer still "
"cut (`finish_reason: length`, or Claude's `max_tokens`) is reported as "
"`truncated`, with the reasoning tokens spent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:303 fb8f4db1b3d246d18b65fa4713badba3
msgid ""
"**Claude specifics:** Opus/Sonnet 5.5 get adaptive thinking (when the "
"feature asks for it), an explicit effort and the server-side refusal "
"fallback (`fallbacks: \"default\"`); other Claude models (Haiku 4.5) get "
"none of these and have no web search. Web turns and turns over 16,000 "
"output tokens are streamed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:309 deef93883987402abccb712256a94f1d
msgid ""
"The features are `product_research` (web + JSON), `reference_suggestion` "
"(JSON), `description_writing` (JSON), `document_search` (web + JSON) and "
"`pdf_extraction` (JSON; the PDF is sent as a document: Claude reads it "
"natively, OpenRouter as a `file` part). `reference_suggestion`'s system "
"prompt holds the full brand, type and key lists and is cached "
"(`cache_control` on Claude; OpenRouter models cache per their provider), "
"so repeated suggestions mostly pay cache reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:317 a46a4095133f45f585e5216d90857a61
msgid ""
"Commercial review (`api/services/review_queue.py`, "
"`api/services/model_sheet.py`, `api/services/product_assist.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:319 ce57306c880c419c9f840156991690dd
msgid ""
"Units reach Airtable without the commercial team (see \"Units of received"
" items\" above); what they review is the **Model**, for the site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:322 e296ebd5aea74d9ba3fcb831a8bac9cc
msgid ""
"**The queue** (`GET /review-queue`): every Model whose `Vérification pour"
" site` is unchecked and that has Units `A vendre` or `Non traité`, or a "
"Variation still `À valider` (a new reference created by operations). "
"Order: Models with Units `A vendre` first, those meant for the site "
"(`to_sell_on_shopify` not `Non`) before the others, by number of Units on"
" sale; then by Units `Non traité`; newest stock first among equals. Each "
"entry has its counts (`a_vendre`, `non_traite`, `non_teste`), `is_new`, "
"`to_sell`, `on_shopify`, `is_accessory`, and what its sheet lacks "
"(`missing`: `description`, `photos`, `dimensions`, `poids`, `shopify`). "
"Reading it pages through the stock (~15 s): it is cached in the process "
"and rebuilt in the background after 5 minutes; a verified Model leaves it"
" at once, an unverified one comes back at the next rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:334 44fdfec27c2f490bbe91b5191e5a3426
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Verifying** (`POST /models/{id}/verify`) needs the Shopify decision "
"(`to_sell_on_shopify`, editable through `PATCH /models/{id}`), then "
"checks `Vérification pour site` and sets every Variation `Statut "
"verification = Vérifié`; a Variation still `À valider` becomes `Validé`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:339 e668324e5d5a4391bbfed6ef10bb37fb
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The sheet (`GET /models/{id}/sheet?all_variations=true`) shows everything"
" to check. Corrections are explicit (`PATCH /models/{id}`) and "
"optimistic: the app sends the values it showed, and a field changed in "
"Airtable meanwhile refuses the whole edit rather than overwriting it. "
"Specifications are edited per Variation (`/variations/{id}/specs`, "
"`/specs/{id}`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:345 59684a4007704c419ede335263bb3f65
msgid "AI help, proposals only:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:347 bfac8a8ed6aa4e45b313178edd2be5e1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**The product's PDF** (`POST /models/{id}/pdf`, `pdf_extraction`): the "
"sales team uploads the PDF they prepared for this model (10 MB max). It "
"is added to the Model's `Documentation` (Airtable's content API, 5 MB "
"max; `attached.reason`: `already_there` / `too_large` / `error` "
"otherwise, `not_asked` with `attach: false`), then the AI reads it with "
"the list of Airtable specification keys and returns the sheet in the web "
"research's shape (`source: \"pdf\"`): descriptions, dimensions, weight, "
"new price, specifications (Airtable spelling when the key exists), "
"`variants` (axis key, value, unit, their own specifications), "
"`unmapped_facts`, `issues` and `confidence` (`identified` is false when "
"there are issues). Only what the PDF states; nothing is written besides "
"the attachment. A proposed variant is created on request with `POST "
"/models/{id}/variants` (`CatalogSync.add_variant`): a new Variation `À "
"valider` with its axis and specifications (idempotent per Model, axis key"
" and value: push key `app-variant:<model>:<key>:<value>`), or, with "
"`convert_variation_id`, the Model's default Variation turned into that "
"variant (refused on Shopify: `on_shopify`; already a variant: "
"`already_variant`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:365 dfcf998de34e496581a0daab7feffcb8
msgid ""
"**Descriptions** (`description_writing`): French, factual, short (one "
"sentence) and long (2-4 paragraphs), from the identity, the "
"specifications and the current texts; a current text about another "
"product is not reused and is reported in `issues`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:369 2a445d8c3837407bb5fbfcbff02deeb5
msgid ""
"**PDF documents** (`document_search`, Celery task `run_document_search`):"
" one web call with structured output (at most 6 documents, kinds "
"`manual`, `service_manual`, `datasheet`, `brochure`, `other`, plus "
"`notes` for the sales team); every link is then fetched (first bytes "
"only, up to 5 redirects followed by hand) and kept only if it is a PDF on"
" a public host (no private, loopback or link-local address, at any hop). "
"The same check runs again before a link is attached to the Model; "
"Airtable then downloads the file from the URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:378 d899f3ca0fb14bb0a2fc329b62e863d6
msgid "Reference suggestion (`api/services/reference_suggestion.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:380 cc8579cac8ce440288a40100127f605a
msgid ""
"Called by the app for one received item (`POST /suggest-reference`): "
"which **existing** Variation it is, else what new reference to create. "
"Never raises for AI reasons: without AI (disabled, limit, unavailable) "
"the heuristic ranking alone is returned with ``ai_error``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:385 c0b0b9d1573246aeac7f9cbf9e5a5f1f
msgid ""
"The catalog index ranks every Variation against what is known of the item"
" (brand, model, serial, seller's product name — for an accessory, also "
"what it was found in — label text) and keeps a shortlist of 12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:388 3f3f0bfacb044320b9aff26862c83149
msgid ""
"The AI (feature ``reference_suggestion``, its chain of AI models; photos "
"if the settings allow: `use_images`, up to `max_images`) returns "
"``matches`` among the numbered candidates with a confidence and a reason,"
" the new-reference fields (brand as in the brand list, model reference, "
"type from the type list, variant axis from the specification keys) and "
"the **serial number** read on the label or photos (labels usually print "
"it ``SN:``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:394 9b93298ee2fe46fc897a5d5485bf2cb7
msgid ""
"**Fallback pass:** when no candidate reaches 0.6 and ``photos_text`` (OCR"
" of the item's other photos) is given, a second call adds that text "
"(``ocr_fallback``, on by default); what only the first pass read is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:397 b8248e61a7894de286b7d095ab941133
msgid ""
"Result: ``match`` (``existing`` from 0.6), ``variations`` (the AI's "
"matches; the heuristic ranking only when no AI answered; ``suggestions`` "
"items), ``new_reference`` (closest existing brands, models and types with"
" confidences; ``brand_proposal`` flagged ``new`` when not in Airtable — "
"created only once the operator confirms, through ``POST /brands``), "
"``read.serial``, ``fallback_used``, ``rationale``, ``ai_call_id`` for "
"feedback, ``ai_model``, ``images_used``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:406 01e63c35fef240e091fd3cf5a271a1e4
msgid "The app keeps the result, so reloading never pays twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:408 c1a1d8df85a04fb79052d8365cd45a12
msgid ""
"**Catalog search** (`CatalogIndex.search_models`): each searched word is "
"matched against the Model's brand, reference, equipment type, Variation "
"names and variant values — whole word 1, start of a word 0.85, inside a "
"word 0.7, across separators 0.65 (`ub90060` in `UB90.060.089`), close "
"spelling 0.5. Every word must match (with 3+ words, all but one, ranked "
"lower); an exact or contained reference adds to the score, popularity "
"breaks ties. \"2424\", \"Rotor\" and \"rotor 2424\" all find Rotor 2424. "
"`suggest_models` turns the item ranking below into up to 3 Models with "
"their best Variation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../catalog_intake.md:417 898b18d706e8491e8bba4f566a8e266a
msgid ""
"**Catalog index** (`api/services/catalog_index.py`): brands, types, "
"Models (with dimensions) and Variations (with unit counts) loaded from "
"Airtable and reloaded in the background when used after 15 minutes "
"(invalidated after pushes and brand / type / spec-type creations). It "
"scores every Variation against the item — brand 0.35, model reference "
"0.45, type 0.08, variant value on the label 0.05, popularity 0.07 — and "
"the top 12 go to the AI as numbered candidates; invented candidate "
"numbers are dropped. This replaces an MCP lookup: the full Variation list"
" is too large for a prompt, the shortlist is not. The number of proposals"
" per list is `reference_suggestion.suggestions` (1-5, default 3)."
msgstr ""

